# Scrapes and translates today's column into ~/published/today.json (builder/build.py).
# Started by darling-build.timer, or now with `scripts/ship.sh build`. Both are meant
# to be installed as systemd user units of the site's user.

[Unit]
Description=darling: scrape, translate and publish today's column

[Service]
Type=oneshot
WorkingDirectory=%h/current/app/builder
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, and optionally TRANSLATOR and CLAUDE_MODEL (deploy/darling.env.example).
EnvironmentFile=-%h/darling.env
# uv has to be installed system-wide, in this PATH.
Environment=PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
# Outside releases, so deploys and rollbacks keep today's column. Every release's
# public/today.json links here, and the real art sits next to it in art/.
Environment=TODAY_JSON=%h/published/today.json
# One venv for all releases, instead of a fresh one inside each release.
Environment=UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT=%h/venv
ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/uv run --frozen --no-dev build.py
# Scraping and translating take a minute at most; a hung run shouldn't block the next one.
TimeoutStartSec=15min
Nice=10
